## Third-party components

Third-party code and references retain their upstream licenses:

- **Gstack** — https://github.com/garrytan/gstack. Vendored skill attribution
  is listed in skills-src/VENDORED.md. The safety runtime restoration below
  additionally includes adapted executable code under Garry Tan's MIT license.
- **Superpowers** — https://github.com/obra/superpowers (concepts referenced
  in simon-tdd / simon-worktree; no code vendored)
- **everything-claude-code** — https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code
  (concepts referenced in simon-instincts / simon-research; no code vendored)

Except for identified third-party components, SimonK contributions are released
under the MIT license above.

## Gstack safety runtime restoration (2026-09-24)

Upstream: https://github.com/garrytan/gstack/tree/b9706f3635b6a545f46fae607ae9d6bcbfb69b91
Pinned commit: b9706f3635b6a545f46fae607ae9d6bcbfb69b91
Original LF-byte SHA-256 (before the explicitly described SimonK adaptations):

- careful/bin/check-careful.sh: 7b04f0b8f409d4ecf166ef45e72eb95ed7c2f37434bd7125e6b403d0f7bf5d42
- careful/bin/hook-extract.sh: 5be66386d4945f27ba52ac3df720a8f84755634de1713eacbd239376050106c9
- freeze/bin/check-freeze.sh: 97e6013a990911ef544e4e80fc464560286e298d85ffbdf391b860e9910376f4

Careful rebase (2026-10-03, hub decision D-56): careful was re-based on gstack
v1.91.9.0, commit 96764e80a641e28141ec8297223768029f5bf483, whose two careful
files above are byte-identical (same SHA-256) to the pinned commit. Added from
that commit, unchanged except for a leading attribution comment block:

- bin/gstack-slug: 67bb219bc2e57dedbf33421802607b5e6e639e5905f21caa18af56398058a5c8
  (vendored as skills-src/careful/bin/gstack-slug.sh)

Freeze/unfreeze/guard rebase (2026-10-03, hub decision D-62 step A2): based on
the installed gstack v1.91.9 copies (the release D-56 pins to the commit above).
Upstream LF-byte SHA-256 of the files taken:

- freeze/bin/check-freeze.sh: fa1ee8bf2e7d7d2bb95b3cf81b5bdd65967e9c92c9d9cd2eb90bdd94969c33b4
  (adapted; SimonK deltas listed in its header and below)
- freeze/bin/freeze-state.sh: ee14660e8dd6fedb1e6673fccffa9ff1740047955ef5b59d58d246ad1dccebf5
  (vendored as skills-src/freeze/bin/freeze-state.sh, unchanged except for a
  leading attribution comment block)

These files reside under skills-src/. They are adapted, not byte-identical
copies. Local changes preserve the current SimonK skill contracts:

- careful follows upstream tiers: HIGH patterns deny; MEDIUM destructive
  families and shell obfuscation ask. HIGH (simple commands only) covers
  recursive delete of the filesystem root, a drive root (also the Windows/MSYS
  spellings /c, /c/*, /mnt/c, C:, C:\, C:/*) or the home directory or its direct
  contents (~/*, $HOME/*), including cmd.exe rd|del /s and PowerShell
  Remove-Item -Recurse launched from Bash against a drive root or home, plus
  force-push to the default branch (D-62 A1). The PowerShell tool (D-62
  minimal B) is checked deny-only: recursive delete of a drive root or home
  (HOME or USERPROFILE spellings), Format-Volume, Clear-Disk, Initialize-Disk,
  Remove-Partition and a force-push to the default branch deny; everything
  else is allowed, never asked. Every internal hook failure denies: the
  EXIT-trap backstop on unexpected runtime errors, a missing/broken/outdated
  helper, empty or invalid JSON, no JSON parser, a Bash or PowerShell payload
  without a usable command, an unknown hook mode argument, baseline matcher
  errors (distinguished from clean non-matches) and an unresolvable
  per-project slug. Other tools are recognised by tool_name and allowed. Both
  SKILL hook commands are anchored to $HOME/.claude/skills/careful because
  ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} was measured unset in frontmatter hooks; the plugin
  candidate projection runs both entries through the safety runtime (the
  PowerShell entry as its careful-powershell policy). This is not a security
  sandbox and never grants permission to execute a destructive action.
- The shared state reader matches existing writers exactly:
  ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA:-$HOME/.gstack}. GSTACK_HOME remains analytics-only for
  these hooks; it does not override the boundary writer's chosen state root.
- Missing/empty/wrong-type required input and NUL fail closed (deny for careful,
  deny for an active freeze). File paths reject control characters before Bash
  can silently strip trailing newlines. Only an absent state file is an inactive freeze;
  invalid state, unreadable state, broken links and unresolved paths deny.
- Freeze path resolution requires an existing parent; newly created nested
  directories are conservatively denied until their parents exist. The helper
  does not fall back to lexical prefix matching after a resolution failure.
  Existing directory/root boundaries resolve directly, with root-aware joining.
- After physical resolution, Git Bash mount aliases use cygpath for comparison
  (/tmp and /c can denote the same directory).
- freeze (D-62) normalizes the boundary and the Edit/Write file_path the same
  way: Windows drive paths (C:\ and C:/) become /c/ via cygpath -u (pure-bash
  fallback without cygpath), the parent is resolved physically, mount aliases
  are folded with cygpath -am, and the comparison is case-insensitive on
  Windows. Relative, drive-relative, root-relative, UNC/device paths, a ".."
  segment and any failed conversion deny instead of falling back to the cwd
  (upstream joined such paths to the cwd and so allowed out-of-boundary edits
  while the cwd was inside the boundary). An empty boundary denies (upstream
  allowed it). The freeze, unfreeze and guard SKILL hook/setup commands are
  anchored to $HOME/.claude/skills/<skill> because ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} was
  measured unset in frontmatter hooks; boundaries are written and cleared only
  through the vendored freeze-state.sh. This does not certify host hook dispatch.

Validated scope: scripts/tests/test_safety_hooks.py exercises actual Bash
subprocesses, isolated home/state and flat source-package materialization.
It only passes commands as stdin data; it never executes them. Dependencies:
Bash and POSIX utilities, plus python3 or Node for JSON parsing. Optional
per-project custom patterns use the vendored careful/bin/gstack-slug.sh;
skills-src/careful/bin/test_check_careful.py covers the careful contract and
skills-src/freeze/bin/test_check_freeze.py the freeze, unfreeze and guard
contract (Windows path forms, freeze-state.sh busy lock and clear).
The plugin candidate's freeze/bin/safety_runtime.py (hub decision D-62
follow-up 5) passes a leaf decision through unchanged with its reason: allow,
careful ask, careful or freeze deny. Its own failures (no Git Bash, bad state,
bad, oversized or out-of-contract leaf output, timeout) deny for both careful
and freeze; it never downgrades a deny to ask.

NOT a completed activation or installation: separated Core/Stack plugin sibling
dependencies, plugin-specific state sharing with unfreeze, session ownership and
cleanup, SKILL hook command quoting/variable availability, native Windows file
paths, and Claude/Codex host enforcement remain unverified or known incomplete.
The candidate runtime/host/installation readiness flags therefore remain false.
Current SKILL activation claims must not be treated as host-verification evidence.

